# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data must never be committed. CareScribe writes only de-identified
# text to disk, into carescribe/output/deidentified/ — but a de-identified
# clinical document is still not something to push to a git remote, and a
# reviewer may have marked identifiers "Keep" on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
carescribe/output/
*.deid.txt
*_deidentified.txt
*_deidentified.md
*_carenote.txt
*_carenote.md
*_carenote_PHI.txt
*_carenote_PHI.md
patient_data/
phi/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# graphify knowledge graph.
#
# graph.json / GRAPH_REPORT.md / graph.html ARE committed — they are the map a
# new session (or a new contributor) starts from. Only the machine-specific and
# local-only bits are ignored: .graphify_python and .graphify_root hold absolute
# paths to this machine's conda env, and cost.json is a local token tally.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/20*/
